lines = {
"puca_watch": {"text": "Still no sign of Tamlin. Then something moved by the hedges.", "who": ""},
"puca_window": {"text": "Below my window, by the hedges: my father. Under-dressed for winter, stooped on his cane.", "who": ""},
"puca_come_down": {"text": "Father, out there in the cold. I had to go down to him.", "who": ""},
"puca_beckons": {"text": "He beckoned, and limped on toward the gates.", "who": ""},
"tamlin_going": {
"text": "Going somewhere?",
"who": "Tamlin"
},
"tamlin_look_again": {
"text": "Why don't you look again?",
"who": "Tamlin"
},
"tamlin_puca": {
"text": "A puca. It shows you what you want and lures you somewhere remote. Then it eats you, slowly.",
"who": "Tamlin"
}
}
extra_require = PackedStringArray()
invented = PackedStringArray("tamlin_puca")
canon = "Ch10-11 (keeper, 2026-11-01, 04-creatures/puca.md). Silent and visual: the father never speaks; he limps on his cane, beckoning, to the open gates. Tamlin: 'Going somewhere?' then 'Why don't you look again?' It shifts: a pale bow and quiver, a laden pack, her sisters huddled weeping, her father again; it shimmers and darts away. tamlin_puca paraphrases what he tells her (X wording). The sobbing sound and the glimpsed true form are X. Hedge mark = SitePlan.PUCA_GARDEN_SPOT relative to the garden_gate anchor."
